This is the Hash Code 2015 "Optimize a Data Center" problem. The approach is a greedy placement followed by a greedy pool assignment.

**Placement.** Sort servers by capacity/size ratio, descending. Within each row, the free slots form segments between unavailable slots. For each server in that order, put it in the row with the most free space that has a segment big enough, which spreads capacity evenly across rows. A first-fit within the row's segments works. To keep it fast, each row holds a list of segments (start, remaining length), and a server is placed at the start of the first segment that fits. With up to 1e6 servers and 1000 rows, scanning all rows for each server is too slow.

Instead, process servers in sorted order and cycle through rows in round-robin fashion. For each server, try rows starting from the current pointer and take the first row that has a segment that fits. Then advance the pointer past that row. To keep it cheap, per row I keep a pointer into its segment list, skipping segments with remaining length 0. A segment too small for this server is not discarded, since a smaller server may fit later. Scanning a row's segments could be long, so I limit scanning cost by checking a per-row maximum remaining segment length. Computing that maximum costs O(segments) per placement. That is acceptable, because the number of placements is at most R·S = 1e6 and the segments per row are usually few. The worst case is many segments, such as alternating unavailable slots, but then each segment has length 1 and the scan finds a fit quickly or fails. I accept this risk and cap the number of rows tried per server at R.

**Pool assignment.** Take the placed servers in descending capacity order. For each server, choose the pool that has the lowest guaranteed capacity, breaking ties by the lowest capacity in the server's row. A pool's guaranteed capacity is total minus the max row sum. Evaluating all pools for each server costs P·M, which is too heavy. Instead, assign by a heap: pop the pool with the lowest current guaranteed capacity (total − maxrow), and give it the server, choosing from the remaining servers the one that sits in a row where the pool is weakest. Simplified: for the popped pool, place the next largest server, which keeps the work to O(M log P). To make it row-aware, I process servers in descending order and, for each, pick the pool from the heap. Per-pool row sums are stored as a P×R array of ints, 1e6 entries, which is fine. After assigning, I update the pool's total and max row sum, then push it back to the heap.

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main(){
    int R,S,U,P,M;
    scanf("%d %d %d %d %d",&R,&S,&U,&P,&M);
    vector<vector<char>> bad(R,vector<char>(S,0));
    for(int i=0;i<U;i++){int r,s;scanf("%d %d",&r,&s);bad[r][s]=1;}
    vector<int> z(M),c(M);
    for(int i=0;i<M;i++)scanf("%d %d",&z[i],&c[i]);
    // segments
    vector<vector<pair<int,int>>> seg(R);
    for(int r=0;r<R;r++){
        int s=0;
        while(s<S){
            if(bad[r][s]){s++;continue;}
            int e=s;
            while(e<S&&!bad[r][e])e++;
            seg[r].push_back({s,e-s});
            s=e;
        }
    }
    vector<int> ord(M);
    iota(ord.begin(),ord.end(),0);
    stable_sort(ord.begin(),ord.end(),[&](int a,int b){
        return (long long)c[a]*z[b]>(long long)c[b]*z[a];
    });
    vector<int> pr(M,-1),ps(M,-1),pp(M,-1);
    int ptr=0;
    for(int id:ord){
        int zz=z[id];
        for(int t=0;t<R;t++){
            int r=(ptr+t)%R;
            bool done=false;
            for(auto&sg:seg[r]){
                if(sg.second>=zz){
                    pr[id]=r;ps[id]=sg.first;
                    sg.first+=zz;sg.second-=zz;
                    done=true;break;
                }
            }
            if(done){ptr=(r+1)%R;break;}
        }
    }
    vector<int> placed;
    for(int id:ord)if(pr[id]>=0)placed.push_back(id);
    stable_sort(placed.begin(),placed.end(),[&](int a,int b){return c[a]>c[b];});
    vector<int> rs((size_t)P*R,0),tot(P,0),mx(P,0);
    typedef pair<int,int> pi;
    priority_queue<pi,vector<pi>,greater<pi>> pq;
    for(int p=0;p<P;p++)pq.push({0,p});
    for(int id:placed){
        auto t=pq.top();pq.pop();
        int p=t.second;
        pp[id]=p;
        int r=pr[id];
        rs[(size_t)p*R+r]+=c[id];
        tot[p]+=c[id];
        mx[p]=max(mx[p],rs[(size_t)p*R+r]);
        pq.push({tot[p]-mx[p],p});
    }
    for(int i=0;i<M;i++){
        if(pr[i]<0)puts("x");
        else printf("%d %d %d\n",pr[i],ps[i],pp[i]);
    }
}
```
